# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own keys. .env.local is
# gitignored and must stay that way: Google and Groq scan GitHub (private
# repos included) and revoke any key they find, which silently turns search off.
#
# Hosting: .env.local is not read by Vercel. Add the same variables in the
# project's Environment Variables settings (Production) and redeploy.
#
# Every community, place, event, and person shown in Onclave comes from live
# search, and the server opens each result's page to confirm it exists before
# showing it. Without a key that can search the web (GEMINI_API_KEY or
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY) those lists stay mostly empty.

# Gemini API key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# It starts with "AIza". A key that starts with "AQ." is a Vertex AI key and
# is rejected by this API. The key needs Google Search grounding enabled,
# which on some accounts requires billing on the linked Google Cloud project.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Gemini model. Defaults to gemini-3.6-flash.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# Optional but recommended: OpenRouter, one account that reaches many models.
# Its web plugin lets any model read live search results, so it can do the
# web search when Gemini is out of quota. Searches are billed per result on
# top of the model's price, so check OpenRouter's current pricing.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys (it starts with "sk-or-v1-").
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the OpenRouter model. Defaults to anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# Optional backup for when Gemini fails. Groq has no web access, so it can
# only suggest candidates from memory; each is still checked against its real
# page before it is shown. It also drafts messages if Gemini is unavailable.
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Groq model. Defaults to openai/gpt-oss-120b.
GROQ_MODEL=
